The `MaybeNever` class is a trivial, constant‑time implementation that merely registers a never‑disposing disposable with the observer. It contains no computational logic, state changes, or I/O that could exhibit performance characteristics worth measuring. Benchmarking such a no‑op would only capture framework overhead, which is already well‑understood and not specific to this class. Therefore, generating a JMH benchmark for this code is unnecessary.